CYC.LESSONS[5] = [
  { id: 'fivevaults', title: 'Same bytes, five tasks',
    body: 'KV bytes per token = 2 × layers × kv_heads × head_dim × bytes. Llama-3-70B in bf16: 320 KiB per token, 40 GiB at 128k. Decode is a memory-bound loop that re-reads the cache every step: 40 GiB at 4.8 TB/s is ~9 ms per token before a single weight is read, so <b>bandwidth is the requirement</b>, and capacity caps batch size, which is throughput. The same bytes face five tasks with five requirement sheets: resident in HBM (online, random access, decoder is the attention kernel), offloaded to host DRAM with sparse gather (PCIe is the channel), parked in cold storage (encode once, the entropy coder returns), streamed over a network (every byte is latency), or evicted (a two-level quantizer). Each task empties and fills different stages.',
    takeaway: 'Read the task before the data. The data did not change between the five tasks; every stage did.' },
  { id: 'keysvalues', title: 'Keys are not values',
    body: 'Keys have a few channels with 20× the magnitude of the rest, stable across tokens; values do not. So KIVI quantizes keys per channel and values per token: reverse the axes at 2 bits and GSM8K on Llama-2-13B drops from 20.8 to <b>0.00</b>. RoPE then rotates each channel pair by a position-dependent angle, smearing each outlier between two channels so that per-channel statistics stop being stationary and the low-rank structure of keys disappears. Hence pre-RoPE storage: keep keys before the rotation and re-apply it inside the kernel (KVQuant: 3-bit perplexity 7.05 → 6.23 from this alone). Pre-RoPE keys of a long prompt are low-rank (ShadowKV keeps rank 160 of 1024); values are not, so ShadowKV factors the keys and offloads the values. QuaRot takes the other road: rotate q and k by the same Hadamard after RoPE, which preserves q·k and flattens the outliers.',
    demo: 'unrope', duel: 8, takeaway: 'Per-channel K, per-token V. Undo RoPE or rotate both sides. Keys are low-rank, values are not.' },
  { id: 'jointentropy', title: 'Joint entropy',
    body: 'Channels of a key or value vector are correlated, so their joint entropy grows slower than the sum of their marginals: <b>H(X₁,…,X₈) ≤ H(X₁) + … + H(X₈)</b>, with equality only if they are independent. The gap is mutual information. A scalar quantizer codes each channel alone and pays the marginals; a codebook over 4-8 channels pays the joint. Coupled Quantization gets 1 bit per channel with LLaMA-2-13B perplexity 6.55 where 1-bit scalar quantization gives 4,709; weighting the k-means by Fisher information moves the error to where the loss does not care. CommVQ builds the codebook from 2×2 scaled rotations so it commutes with RoPE and the query-codebook product is computed once per step. This is the lesson of billion-scale vector search (correlated dimensions are where VQ wins) arriving in HBM, with the codebook shipped in the checkpoint.',
    demo: 'coupled', duel: 9, takeaway: 'Sum of marginal entropies − joint entropy = mutual information = what a scalar quantizer pays twice.' },
  { id: 'softmaxaudience', title: 'The softmax is the audience',
    body: 'Every lossy codec has a perceptual model: a description of what the reader will not notice. Here the reader is attention, and <b>0.5% of keys carry 90% of a query\'s attention mass</b>. Distortion on a token the softmax weights at ~0 costs nothing; distortion on the first token (attention sink) or the newest 128 is amplified, so those stay in fp16 (KIVI\'s residual window alone moves GSM8K from 12.2 to 20.8). Which tokens matter changes every step, which splits the field: selection with a lossless backing copy (ShadowKV, SpeCache, HiSparse) never forgets, eviction (SnapKV, H2O) does. Two systems facts shape both: FlashAttention never writes the N×N score matrix to HBM, so an importance model must rebuild its signal from a proxy; and paged allocators free a 16-token block only when it is empty, so eviction without compaction frees nothing.',
    demo: 'spotlight', takeaway: 'Importance replaces masking. Selection saves compute; only eviction or offload saves memory, and eviction needs compaction.' },
  { id: 'leavinggpu', title: 'When the cache leaves the GPU',
    body: 'Inside HBM the Entropy coding stage is empty in every method: the attention kernel must find element i by arithmetic. The moment the cache is stored or shipped, every classical stage returns. KVTC is a JPEG for KV: undo RoPE, one PCA basis shared across all layers and heads (2.4% of the model\'s parameters, shipped as side information), reverse water-filling bit allocation per coordinate, uniform quantization, then DEFLATE: 18-22× with GSM8K unchanged, and the entropy coder alone adds <b>1.23×</b>. Decompressing takes 380 ms against 3,098 ms to recompute. CacheGen does the same over a network: anchor-token deltas (2.4-2.9× lower variance than raw values), layer-dependent step sizes, and arithmetic coding with one probability table per layer and channel, 3.5-4.3× smaller than uniform quantization. The production shortcut, TensorRT-LLM cold pages, is just NVFP4 applied as a page migrates and undone as it returns.',
    demo: 'waterline', duel: 11, takeaway: 'Random access gone ⇒ entropy coder back. Same transform-quantize-code recipe as JPEG, on activations.' },
  { id: 'architects', title: 'The biggest shrink was never a codec',
    body: 'The largest reductions of KV memory happened at model design time. GQA shares 8 KV heads among 64 query heads: 8× fewer things to store. MLA caches one 512-dim latent plus a 64-dim RoPE key per token per layer instead of two 128×128 tensors: <b>576 elements instead of 32,768</b>, equal to GQA with 2.25 groups, and the up-projections are absorbed into W_Q and W_O so the latent is attended to directly. DeepSeek-V4 compresses along the token axis too: 30 layers cache a learned weighted sum of each 4 tokens, 31 layers one entry per 128 tokens, 9.6 GiB per million-token sequence instead of 83.9. RoPE is the one structure that refused to compress, hence the separate small positional key. Everything the codec stages do afterwards works on what the architects left.',
    demo: 'mla', takeaway: 'Transform baked in at training time: zero encode, zero decode, zero choice afterwards.' },
];

